A('**Result: it stays near the contiguous value. The drift is real and the metric is measuring it.** Purged folds leave the anti-predictive draws where they were (0.380 → 0.358 at Track A, 0.355 → 0.326 at walk-forward; on the quoted test-block pairs, 0.403 → 0.195 on the draws where it fits) and only 1.0% / 0.3% of them cross 0.5, against 98.8% / 90.1% under shuffled folds. The share of the whole null below 0.5 goes **up** under purging (NIFTY50 Track A 20.9% → 25.6%). The shuffled-fold values near 0.62–0.67 are what leakage through overlapping windows produces, not what a corrected estimator recovers. I proceeded, as both outcomes were results.\n')
